IncidentBot: :rotating_light: Paging eng-oncall: Emergency rate-surge detection for /v1/generate (region: us-west-2). Increased error-5xx and token latency spikes observed. Root alert at 1905001234.

maria (oncall): seeing huge spike in 5xx from a small set of API keys, looks like a client batch job hammering us. 95th latency up to 2.1s. customer impact: intermittent failures and token throttling.

sam (sdk): can we do a fast client-side mitigation? recommend issuing updated runtime-config that changes default retry behavior + idempotency guidance.

akshay (runtime): we're already triggering emergency autoscale but queuing increases. I'm going to apply a short-term service-level throttling rule: reduce per-key RPS to 20 for new connections, keep existing pinned sessions at current rates for 2 minutes to avoid stomp. Applying now.

maria (oncall): ok apply throttle and also temporarily disable streaming responses for anonymous keys (to cut down on long-lived connections). akshay, please confirm when toggle hits prod.

akshay (runtime): toggle deployed to canary then prod at 1905001260. streaming disabled for anonymous keys.

jen (support): prepping a customer-facing note for targeted impacted keys. CC'ing account owners for enterprise customers.

sam (sdk): SDK mitigations we should push immediately (short patch + advisory):
- default retry policy: exponential backoff with full jitter (base=200ms, cap=10s, retries=5)
- honor Retry-After header from API and treat 429/503 as retryable
- add idempotency-key header in all create-style calls; if present, SDK should re-send on network error but not on explicit 4xx
- short-circuit streaming by falling back to non-streaming endpoint when streaming fails repeatedly

sam (sdk): quick JS snippet to illustrate new behavior for reference:
```js
// simple exponential backoff with full jitter
async function retryWithJitter(fn, retries = 5) {
  for (let i = 0; i < retries; i++) {
    try {
      return await fn();
    } catch (err) {
      const retryAfter = parseInt(err.headers?.['retry-after']) || 0;
      if (err.status && err.status >= 400 && err.status < 500 && err.status !== 429) throw err;
      if (i === retries - 1) throw err;
      const base = 200;
      const cap = 10000;
      const exp = Math.min(cap, base * Math.pow(2, i));
      const wait = Math.random() * exp + retryAfter * 1000;
      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, wait));
    }
  }
}
```

sam (sdk): also adding example header usage: `Idempotency-Key: <uuidv4()>` and `X-Client-Retry: 1` to help us debug if needed.

akshay (runtime): we'll also return clearer Retry-After on 429s and include `X-Server-Load: high` header for telemetry. Please make SDK map the Retry-After if present.

maria (oncall): support, coordinate with the account owners to suggest immediate client-side pauses for any scheduled batch jobs. We should also offer a temporary per-customer quota bump on request if they can switch to non-streaming calls.

jen (support): noted. drafting short message template: "We detected elevated request volumes from your API key causing intermittent failures. To reduce errors, please pause scheduled jobs and upgrade to our dedicated capacity or enable non-streaming mode. If you need a temporary quota increase while you migrate, reply here."

sam (sdk): planning a point release patch (v3.2.1) with the new retry defaults and idempotency helper. Will cut PR now and tag for hotfix channel. Jetty: please hold until I publish changelog then we can trigger a quick publish.

maria (oncall): handoff to night oncall in 20m. akshay, confirm if any further actions for routing/fallbacks.

akshay (runtime): will enable model-fallback to a smaller-context model for best-effort requests after 5s queue wait; that reduces GPU pressure. Implemented at 1905001450.

sam (sdk): adding to advisory: recommend SDK users set `maxRetries=5`, `baseBackoffMs=200`, and `preferStreaming=false` if they hit issues. Provide sample curl for idempotency header:
```
curl -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/v1/generate \n  -H "Authorization: Bearer $KEY" \n  -H "Idempotency-Key: 3f8b2c9a-..." \n  -d '{"prompt":"..."}'
```

maria (oncall): good. I'm going to create an incident summary and classify impact as "partial degradation - limited customer subset". Will include mitigation timeline, SDK advisory link, and support template.

jen (support): sending the first batch of messages to affected customers now.

sam (sdk): PR: https://github.com/redwood/sdk/pull/521 (hotfix, retry/idempotency defaults). please review quickly @maria @akshay.

akshay (runtime): review done, nothing blocking. maria, when you close the thread later, please include the permanent mitigations: improved per-key anomaly detection and a safe-mode that forces streaming->polling fallback automatically.

maria (oncall): will do. handoff note: night oncall is @linh (cc). leaving thread open for any follow-ups.

IncidentBot: Incident acknowledged by maria at 1905001580.
